# Project: Oratos

## What this is
An AI-powered business operating system for small/medium companies.
CEOs insert his company information, manage collaborators and tasks,
and interact with an AI that knows the entire business context.

## Stack
- Next.js 14 (App Router)
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Supabase (database + auth + storage)
- n8n (AI agent orchestration)
- Vercel (deployment)
- Open AI (agents)

## Language Rules
- All UI text, labels, buttons, placeholders, messages, and content must be in **Portuguese (PT-BR)**
- All code (variables, functions, components, files, types) must be in **English**
- Database table and column names are in **English**
- Comments in code can be in English — be consistent within the same file

## Architecture
- Multi-tenant: every table has company_id, enforced via Supabase RLS
- Auth: Supabase Auth (CEO signs up, collaborators are invited)
- AI: n8n agent with tools that query Supabase views
- Storage: Supabase Storage for uploaded documents

## Database tables
- Always read src/lib/supabase/schema.md to understand the current database schema

## Styling Rules
- Always use the design tokens defined in `src/app/globals.css`
- Never use hardcoded colors like `#C9A84C` or `hsl(...)` directly in components
- Always import lucide react icons, never use svg
- Always use semantic Tailwind classes that reference CSS variables:
  ```tsx
  // ✅ correct
  className="bg-background text-foreground"
  className="bg-card border-border"
  className="text-primary bg-primary/10"

  // ❌ wrong
  className="bg-[#0B1220] text-[#EEF1F8]"
  className="bg-yellow-500"
  ```

## Code Quality Rules
- No `console.log` in production code — use proper error handling
- No commented-out code blocks — delete unused code
- No hardcoded user IDs, API keys, or secrets in code — use `.env.local`
- Keep components small and focused — if a component exceeds ~150 lines, split it
- Reuse components from `components/shared/` before creating new ones
- Always add loading and empty states to data-fetching components
- Dont import and use client components into server components

## Key rules
- Always use TypeScript
- Always use Tailwind for styling
- Always use Supabase RLS — never expose data across companies
- App Router only — no pages directory
- Server components by default, client components only when needed
- Never hardcode colors — always use the design tokens above